From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:57:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/38] fs: sharedfs: inode numbers carry the generation

An inode number is the index slot plus the low half of the entry's
generation. A slot reused for another file while the guest still holds
the old inode now gets a distinct inode instead of ESTALE, and the host
refuses a request that names a stale entry. Events about entries the
guest has not opened instantiate them first, as `fsnotify_parent` has a
child to report on: a non-dirent event delivered to the directory alone
would arrive without its name.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
